      "writtenOn": "2023-01-25T22:12:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are different things. The \"target peak level\" sets the maximum level of output signal peaks in the time domain. The output signal has the maximum of 0 dBFS, and peaks need to be lower than it by X dB, and the X is set by `targetLevelDbFs`. The \"maximum gain\" is the maximum amount of amplification which the effect is allowed to apply. Thus, \"peak\" is absolutely not a synonym of \"max\" here.",
